course: dictionary
lesson: 14937
title: Patterns that repeat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Regularity is a noun. It describes how something happens again and again, in the same way or at the same times. The root word is regular, and the ending -ity turns that quality into a thing you can name.
explain: «The bus comes every ten minutes, with clockwork regularity.» A clock ticks in exact steps, so clockwork regularity means the bus is always on time and never changes its pattern.
explain: Regularity can also describe even, neat shapes. «The regularity of the square's sides made it easy to draw.» Every side is the same length, so the shape follows a clear pattern. Scientists look for regularities too: patterns they can count on.
fact: Regularity means the quality of happening at the same times or in the same way again and again.
fact: «Accidents happen there with worrying regularity.» This means they happen often, and in a pattern.
fact: In maths, a regular polygon has equal sides and equal angles, so it shows regularity.
fact: Scientists look for regularities, which are patterns, in their results.
fact: Useful phrases: with regularity, with clockwork regularity, and the regularity of meals.
exercise: «The train leaves the station with great regularity.» What does regularity suggest? | It happens only once a year | *It happens often and at steady times | It is very late and never runs | It is loud and fast
exercise: «The regularity of the square's sides makes it a regular shape.» What does regularity mean here? | Sharp, pointed corners only | Lots of bright colours | Wobbly, uneven edges | *Equal sides and a clear pattern
exercise: Mia says regularity means messy. Is she right? | No, it means very loud | Yes, it means untidy and muddled | *No, it means steady and repeating | Yes, it means very late
test: «Meals were eaten at the same time each day, with great regularity.» What does regularity mean here? | Eating only once a week | Being loud at dinner | Being very hungry | *Happening at steady, repeated times
test: Which shape shows regularity best? | A wiggly line with no pattern | A blob of spilt paint | A tangled ball of string | *A square with four equal sides and equal angles
exam: Scientists found a regularity in their results. What does this mean? | A result that is always zero | A bright colour in the lab | A mistake that cannot be fixed | *A pattern that repeats
